Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured after the two physics commits: on WGS-84 with J2 the stack weighs
0.31 % more at Plesetsk than the old sphere model had it (9.821 against
9.791 m/s²; Somigliana's normal gravity is 9.821), and the 4° kick, half a
degree under the kick that broke every Angara row up (4.5° at 23cb4cf),
broke `angaraa5/leo/25` up at T+202 s (q 46 kPa). Fleet rows, point mass:

  kick   leo/25          sso/25  gto/25  gto/50  gto/90   (Δv left, m/s)
  4°     breaks up       3098    3443    2625    1796
  3.75°  3575            3085    3441    2621    1743
  3.5°   3632            3028    3311    2619    1738
  4.5°   every row breaks up

3.5° is half a degree under the new edge, as 4° was under the old, and
every row that passed at 23cb4cf passes (131 of 131 gated rows; 156 of
222 accepted, as before). Through the vehicle's own `guidanceDefaults`
(docs/PHYSICS.md §5.2); the six-DOF kick (8°, guidanceDefaultsSixDof) is
not touched. The D01 identity fixture is re-recorded for it with the
other named re-records.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018CKDnUSFqs1bpw8C2bZmPj
